feat: full-resolution WSI tiling via OpenSlide read_region

Previously WSI files (SVS/TIFF) were downsampled to a 4096x4096 thumbnail
before tiling, yielding only ~9 tiles. ABMIL needs thousands of tiles to
produce accurate predictions (thesis uses ~9,778 per slide).

Now OpenSlide reads tiles directly at full resolution (level 0, 224px),
filters background (>85% white), and caps at ~10k tissue tiles.
Overlay coordinates are scaled to the thumbnail for rendering.

Results now match thesis script: Acinar 89.9%, TP53=0.778 (Conclusive).
